= pH — Simple =

'''pH''' is a way of describing how acidic or basic a solution is.

The pH scale is logarithmic: changing pH by one unit corresponds to a factor of ten in the activity of hydrogen ions. Acidic solutions have lower pH than more basic solutions under comparable conditions.

pH is not just a direct count of hydrogen ions. Scientists use calibrated instruments and standards to estimate it, and temperature and the type of solution matter.

The way acids and bases respond in a mixture is related to [[Chemical equilibrium|chemical equilibrium]].

